  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Write a program to calculate the sum of the digits present in an alphanumeric string.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains an integer, T, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach of the next T lines contains a string consisting of lowercase/uppercase English letters, along with digits 0 to 9. (There shall be no space in the string)\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case, print the sum of digits in each string.",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= T <= 20",
      "1 <= length of each string <= 1000",
      "Strings contain only printable ASCII characters; no spaces."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "First line contains an integer T, the number of test cases. Each of the next T lines contains a non‑empty alphanumeric string (letters, digits and other printable ASCII characters) without spaces.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, output a single integer — the sum of all decimal digits present in the corresponding string.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\nHel#284!lo23Chef",
        "output": "19",
        "explanation": "Digits are 2,8,4,2,3; their sum is 2+8+4+2+3=19."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n1234567890",
        "output": "45",
        "explanation": "Sum of digits 1 through 9 plus 0 equals 45."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\nabc123def456",
        "output": "21",
        "explanation": "Digits 1,2,3,4,5,6 sum to 21."
      }
    ]
  },
