  "solution": {
    "approach": "For each test case we scan the given string character by character. Whenever a character lies between '0' and '9' we convert it to its numeric value by subtracting the character '0' and add it to a running sum. After processing the whole string we output the sum. This linear scan is optimal because every character must be examined at least once.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(L) per test case, where L is the length of the string. Overall O(total length of all strings).",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) extra space besides the input string.",
    "code": {
      "C": "",
      "C++": "",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;public class Main{public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception{BufferedReader br=new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));int T=Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());StringBuilder sb=new StringBuilder();for(int t=0;t<T;t++){String s=br.readLine();int sum=0;for(int i=0;i<s.length();i++){char c=s.charAt(i);if(c>='0'&&c<='9'){sum+=c-'0';}}sb.append(sum);if(t<T-1) sb.append('\\n');}System.out.print(sb.toString());}}",
      "Python3": "",
      "JavaScript": ""
    },
